{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509871-what-would-you-like-implemented-into-m5","id":1509871,"title":"What would you like implemented into M5?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-04-27T10:14:34-07:00","id":1509871,"title":"What would you like implemented into M5?","content":"Me personally, I would like it if they brought back the Foundation and Pillar system from DA:M, of course updated to fit the modern age. I would also like it if they could simplify the Umbra a bit to make it a little easier to understand, for example, combining the Underworlds and Astral Reaches into one and give an explanation of how there is no difference betweem Mind and Soul, or something like that, maybe move aspects of the underworld such as Grandmother to the Middle Umbra. I think it would be cool if they made reality less defined by consensus and encouraged the players to uncover the truth of reality by solving occult mysteries.<br /> <br /> This post actually explained how the Pillar system could be implemented into MTA: <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/mage-the-ascension-but-with-pillars-not-spheres.889868/\" target=\"_blank\">https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?thre...pheres.889868/</a><br /> <br /> What about you?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-27T12:20:50-07:00","id":1509876,"title":"","content":"I respectfully disagree: the Pillar and Foundation system is, for me, one of the worst pitfalls in Mage: the Dark Ages and a huge deterrent for people to play more.<br /> <br /> I would prefer keeping the Nine Spheres and explain them in terms of different cultures, approaches, etc... I mean: Maybe you call them &quot;Whatever and Whatever&quot; and you only have Five elements in your system, but &quot;behind the screen&quot; all Mages use the same magic system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-27T12:36:18-07:00","id":1509879,"title":"","content":"Trying my best to put my WoD5e pessimism aside:<br /> <br /> 1) Foundations, not Pillars, are the things to take from DAM. Foundations give Arete more flavor by Tradition/etc. helping new players to more quickly understand what the rather broad groups of Mage are about. Foundations can be a much more refined implementation of the Predator Archetypes from V5: a carrot to play your character in a specific fashion by getting some bonuses while doing things their preferred way.<br /> <br /> 2) Not mess up stealing Mage: the Awakening 2e's much cleaner implementation of the casting rules. The 13 Practices that are universal so each Sphere has the same broad progression makes it much easier to do free-form magic on the fly, Attainments to better handle some meta-magic mechanics,and making rotes actually matter, are all big things to help make Mage more accessible and more updated to modern game play. One roll casting is also a big improvement, as is putting way more of the Paradox risk on player choices to casting riskily rather than arguments over witnesses.<br /> <br /> 3) Realize that there is no point to Ascension without real world cultures, and figure out a way to handle that. Trying to do what they're doing with W5 where the Garou are global pan-cultural phenomena doesn't work in Ascension. I cannot see M5 succeeding if they try to make the Traditions more like Awakening's Orders, and thus ruin the conflicts that make Ascension matter as a game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-27T12:43:24-07:00","id":1509880,"title":"","content":"I am quite afraid they will indeed remove the consensus reality element of Mage for M5 and that would be a tragedy as it is one of my favorite elements of the game. The whole struggle between the Technocracy and the Traditions really only make sense in the context of a physical reality that is subject to (or even completely determined by) the consensus. <br /> <br /> Instead I would highlight that while Mages know reality has a consensus component, they don't really know how or why it works, they don't know why some things are more resistant to it than others, and they don't know what it means. That leaves plenty of room for occult mysteries and meaning while still letting both the Technocracy and the Traditions be a thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-27T13:23:16-07:00","id":1509884,"title":"","content":"I think they can get away with dropping Consensus (which has been a large impediment to Mage being accessible to wider audiences) as long as they keep the idea of reality being mutable. As long as the ability to change reality is something the factions can be fighting over who gets to say how reality works, switching from Consensus to &quot;unknown powers that be,&quot; can keep the core idea of Ascension alive and distinct without it becoming Awakening with even more unwanted baggage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-27T13:27:25-07:00","id":1509885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509871-what-would-you-like-implemented-into-m5?p=1509879#post1509879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Trying my best to put my WoD5e pessimism aside:<br /> <br /> 1) Foundations, not Pillars, are the things to take from DAM. Foundations give Arete more flavor by Tradition/etc. helping new players to more quickly understand what the rather broad groups of Mage are about. Foundations can be a much more refined implementation of the Predator Archetypes from V5: a carrot to play your character in a specific fashion by getting some bonuses while doing things their preferred way.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is so sensible. The simple fact that the Technocracy uses Enlightenment instead of Arete shows it's already partially in the system. Each Tradition, Craft, or Convention, would have it's own Foundation or Foundations because of their paradigm. Some of the older groups would logically have multiple paradigms and thus multiple Foundations. But one Foundation would probably be dominant among the newer members. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2) Not mess up stealing Mage: the Awakening 2e's much cleaner implementation of the casting rules. The 13 Practices that are universal so each Sphere has the same broad progression makes it much easier to do free-form magic on the fly, Attainments to better handle some meta-magic mechanics,and making rotes actually matter, are all big things to help make Mage more accessible and more updated to modern game play. One roll casting is also a big improvement, as is putting way more of the Paradox risk on player choices to casting riskily rather than arguments over witnesses. </div> </div> </div>The freeform Magic system (which I have always loved) is the thing that most confuses people about Mage. Clarity is always golden. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3) Realize that there is no point to Ascension without real world cultures, and figure out a way to handle that. Trying to do what they're doing with W5 where the Garou are global pan-cultural phenomena doesn't work in Ascension. I cannot see M5 succeeding if they try to make the Traditions more like Awakening's Orders, and thus ruin the conflicts that make Ascension matter as a game. </div> </div> </div>The cultural baggage is a major part of M: The Ascension's charm. It is wonky because of past mistakes, but getting rid of the cultural connections would destroy the game's flavor. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-27T15:45:39-07:00","id":1509904,"title":"","content":"First and foremost: a major goal that I would set for M5 is a drastically reduced page count compared to M20. If you can get it down below 2e, even better.<br /> <br /> That means that you need to be extremely choosey about what goes into it. That <i>alone</i> is reason not to include anything about Foundations or Pillars in the core book. Ditto with things like the Technocratic Sphere variants and Minor Spheres: if anything like that gets included at all, it should come in supplements.<br /> <br /> The tight page count also means that two-page spreads for every Tradition, Convention, and Craft is a non-starter. Instead, I would reserve the two-page spreads for Arcane Approaches, as shown in <b>Mage Made Easy</b>: they're kind of like <b>Awakening</b>'s Paths, but as something that the mage chooses rather than being something pushed on him but a mystical Watchtower or Avatar or whatever. The Societies, meanwhile, get reduced (in the core book) to one-paragraph summaries that specify which Approaches are common in that Society and what makes that Society unique. Basically, complete what M20 started and shift the focus away from the Societies and onto the individual mages: rather than the choice of Society being the thing which defines what your Magick is like, the choice of Society becomes almost an afterthought \u2014 something that you can potentially skip over without hurting the character.<br /> <hr /><br /> For the Magick system, borrow heavily from <b>Awakening 1e</b> (which was written essentially as \u201cwhat we would have liked to write for <b>Ascension</b> of we could have started from scratch\u201d), with the main changes being:<br /> <br /> 1. Practices already has a meaning in <b>Ascension</b>, due to M20; so find another name for what <b>Awakening</b> calls Practices. Likewise, other terms use their <b>Ascension</b> counterpart names (e.g., Arete instead of Gnosis; Spheres instead of Arcana; Effects instead of Spells).<br /> <br /> 2. Entropy instead of Fate and Death. For better or worse, it's deeply rooted in <b>Ascension</b>. That said, I have no problem shifting things around a bit as to what each Sphere deals with.<br /> <br /> 3. Quiescence (the tendency of Sleepers to forget any Magick that they see) isn't a thing. As tempting as it is to keep it, that's always been one of the things that differentiated <b>Mage: the Ascension</b> from <b>Changeling: the Dreaming</b>.<br /> <br /> 4. Borrow the Yantra mechanics from <b>Awakening 2e</b> as a game system for a mage's Instruments, with the tweak that<br /> <br /> 5. The notion of the Supernal and the Abyss gets stripped out. Not that you can't do it that way if you want to; but if you do, it's because that's your Focus; not because it's the fundamental truth about how reality works.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bTo the extent that the subjective nature of reality gets downplayed, it's only in the sense that that's <i>also </i>not guaranteed to be the absolute truth of the setting. I would introduce out in the write-up for the Traditions, as a description of the mechanism that they use to forge bonds among the individual Traditions.<br /> <br /> That is, it's no longer <i>guaranteed </i>to be true; but it still <i>might</i> be true. Which, ironically, makes it more true to the concept than actually making it an absolute truth.<br /> <br /> Rework Paradox around Subtle/Uncanny/Extreme instead of Coincidental/Vulgar/Vulgar with Witnesses. Possibly remove the concept of Witnesses entirely; if not, downplay it to an optional rule. Or ditch Paradox entirely, and replace it with Resonance: Paradox is what some mages call Resonance that bites you. If you go with this approach, there should be four types of Quiet corresponding to the four kinds of Resonance, rather than three that correspond to the Metaphysical Trinity.<br /> <br /> I'd also downplay the Metaphysical Trinity as a holdover from <b>Mage</b>'s earliest days as a sequel to <b>Werewolf</b>, and instead play up the Avatar Essences, kinds of Resonance, and types of Quiet in their place.<br /> <br /> Finally, shift the presentation of the Magick system away from the Spheres and onto the Focus: for instance, put the Focus into Step One of the character creation process; and reference it whenever any aspect of the mage's Magick comes up. You choose your Avatar Essence with your Focus in mind; you choose your Spheres with your Focus in mind; whatever Rotes you know are chosen with your Focus in mind; and so on.<br /> <br /> The first supplements should be sourcebooks for the Traditions, the Technocracy, and the Disparates. In addition to going into much more detail about the individual Societies in those books, this is where you introduce mechanics that are \u201cSociety Secrets\u201d, like something akin to the Technocratic Sphere variants \u2014 although personally, I'd handle those as Merits that take the existing Spheres and tweak what the character can do with them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 04-27-2023, 07:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-27T17:56:01-07:00","id":1509912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The first supplements should be sourcebooks for the Traditions, the Technocracy, and the Disparates. In addition to going into much more detail about the individual Societies in those books, this is where you introduce mechanics that are \u201cSociety Secrets\u201d, like something akin to the Technocratic Sphere variants \u2014 although personally, I'd handle those as Merits that take the existing Spheres and tweak what the character can do with them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe they could implement these as they did with the Loresheets in V5?. I'm not 100% sure if I like that &quot;background-ish&quot; approach for special powers - but your &quot;society&quot; it's kinda part of your background, and the idea of having different &quot;levels&quot; of initiation providing different beneffits (magical secrets, but also social advantages) goes well with the whole mage order trope","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-27T18:58:53-07:00","id":1509914,"title":"","content":"It does, doesn't it? Frankly, I'm unfamiliar with V5; Vampire was never my cup of tea in the first place, and what I've heard about V5 generally doesn't entice me to look into it. So I was unaware of Loresheets. But yeah; I could definitely see the Traditions, Technocracy, and Disparates supplements leaning heavily into Loresheets to provide a mixture of social and arcane benefits.<br /> <br /> And I could see M5's Loresheets incorporating related Merits and Flaws as well, just as V5 has regular Backgrounds that do that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 04-27-2023, 10:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-27T19:37:56-07:00","id":1509917,"title":"","content":"Looking at the structure of V5 and thinking of it in terms of how it would change if it was written for mages rather than vampires: <br /> <br /> <i>Beliefs</i> definitely incorporate what M20 calls Focus, seeing as how Focus is all about what the mage believes about Magick. <i>Convictions</i> ought to somehow relate to your Paradigm: someone who believes that Might Is Right is going to have very different Convictions than someone who believes that It's All Good; Have Faith! <i>Predator Types</i> would be replaced by something like M20's Practices: rather than how you hunt prey, they're about how you work magick. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-28T00:30:32-07:00","id":1509930,"title":"","content":"Keep in mind that H5 and W5 have not hewed so closely to V5's setup. WoD5 is most like DA Revised: a unified core system, but each book goes its own way with how to implement its material. Not as individually divergent as most of the older WoD books, but not the CofD either with some component every supernatural has at least some equivalent to..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-28T04:21:12-07:00","id":1509943,"title":"","content":"To be honest, if they use a system like Awakening I wouldn't even bother trying it. I like some things in it but overall I would rather use Ars Magicka than Awakening.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27335-technoma","name":"Technoma","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-28T05:12:13-07:00","id":1509945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Technoma</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509871-what-would-you-like-implemented-into-m5?p=1509943#post1509943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be honest, if they use a system like Awakening I wouldn't even bother trying it. I like some things in it but overall I would rather use Ars Magicka than Awakening.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find this amusing as I cannot stand the Ars Magica system. I use their books as setting material for Dark Ages Mage (and Mage).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-28T06:13:33-07:00","id":1509947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Technoma</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509871-what-would-you-like-implemented-into-m5?p=1509943#post1509943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be honest, if they use a system like Awakening I wouldn't even bother trying it. I like some things in it but overall I would rather use Ars Magicka than Awakening.</div> </div> </div> </div>My experience with the Awakening Magick system (at least 1e) is that it's largely a carbon copy of the Ascension Magick system, but with improvements. With that in mind, what is it about the Awakening Magick system that you don't like?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-28T19:42:47-07:00","id":1510014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509871-what-would-you-like-implemented-into-m5?p=1509945#post1509945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I find this amusing as I cannot stand the Ars Magica system. I use their books as setting material for Dark Ages Mage (and Mage).</div> </div> </div> </div>I am not saying that it should take the Ars magica rules exactly as written, but i would appreciate some of them. Such as the fact that they, you know, actually exist<br /> Oh, true, i am experienced enough to make up my own interpretations, but a new player can't see a &quot;single sentence&quot; rote and make up the rest of the page that is missing.. or for that matter even realize that it is.<br /> <br /> <br /> By the way, are they actually trying to remove the consensus from mage? Like, how would it work? Would they make it so that the consensus can affect your magick (paradox), but an airplane is its own thing?<br /> <br /> Concerning Pillars, i will admit that i really wish that they included them, but the chance of that is basically 0%. Perhaps as an optional rule? (one may only hope)<br /> That being said, Foundations would still be a step in the nice direction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-29T06:39:25-07:00","id":1510074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509871-what-would-you-like-implemented-into-m5?p=1510014#post1510014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the way, are they actually trying to remove the consensus from mage? Like, how would it work? Would they make it so that the consensus can affect your magick (paradox), but an airplane is its own thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Im also kind of confused about how that would work. Consensus pretty much dictates how reality functions in mage, and paradox is a consequence of breaking the laws of consensual reality. If they removed that, they might have to implement something like backlash from DA:M, which admittedly doesent make sense to do for modern mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-29T07:11:15-07:00","id":1510080,"title":"","content":"I've long been of the opinion that Mage only works if you allow for the possibility that the Consensus <i>isn't </i>the be-all and end-all of reality. M20 addresses this with its Earthly Foundations, where there are certain aspects of reality that will be true even if the locals believe otherwise; though those truths oughtn't be as specific as \u201cthe laws of physics as understood by modern scientists are true\u201d. They should be more broad-brush facts like \u201cthings fall down when you drop them\u201d and \u201cwater flows downhill\u201d. But even things like Newton's observation that the motions of the celestial bodies are described by the same mathematics as falling apples would be more of a Focus element rather than a fundamental truth: scientists see germs through their microscopes because that's what their paradigm says that they'll see, not because germs are actually real. <br /> <br /> I wouldn't want M5 going the route of Awakening and saying that the laws of science are true, and that Magick is a way of overriding them. But there <i>should </i>be something to the effect that the Consensus <i>influences </i>Reality rather than <i>defining </i>it; and the question of what else defines reality besides the Consensus should be left as an open question with several <i>possible </i>answers (e.g., natural laws, or godlike spiritual entities) but nothing conclusive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-29T13:31:42-07:00","id":1510120,"title":"","content":"Thinking of how you could evolve / re-conceptualize lore for M5, and taking some notes from V5, I'd place both the Technocracy and the Traditions as an old crumbling order which is descending into Civil War as the Nephandi reveal the full extent of their infiltration into both Sleeper and Mage society.<br /> <br /> The Consensus start crumbling, and more and more Extraordinary Tech introduced into the Sleeper World backfires and creates potential Widderslainte. Traditions are having a very similar problem, as their efforts in rebuilding a post-Technocracy Consensus collide with millenarism, and more and more Marauders emerge.<br /> <br /> The two main factions are split into a tragic divide: many of their frontline troops are desperately holding out, , but many among the highest ranks are openly thinking Earth as lost. Archmages and Control are openly speaking of evacuating what of the Human Race might be salvaged into Horizon Realms.<br /> <br /> Will you fight to create pockets of &quot;safe and stable&quot; Reality, stopping the descent of your place into madness and corruption, or will you start exploring new realms in which start over?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-29T14:00:32-07:00","id":1510121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509871-what-would-you-like-implemented-into-m5?p=1510080#post1510080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've long been of the opinion that Mage only works if you allow for the possibility that the Consensus <i>isn't </i>the be-all and end-all of reality. M20 addresses this with its Earthly Foundations, where there are certain aspects of reality that will be true even if the locals believe otherwise; though those truths oughtn't be as specific as \u201cthe laws of physics as understood by modern scientists are true\u201d. They should be more broad-brush facts like \u201cthings fall down when you drop them\u201d and \u201cwater flows downhill\u201d. But even things like Newton's observation that the motions of the celestial bodies are described by the same mathematics as falling apples would be more of a Focus element rather than a fundamental truth: scientists see germs through their microscopes because that's what their paradigm says that they'll see, not because germs are actually real.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't want M5 going the route of Awakening and saying that the laws of science are true, and that Magick is a way of overriding them. But there <i>should </i>be something to the effect that the Consensus <i>influences </i>Reality rather than <i>defining </i>it; and the question of what else defines reality besides the Consensus should be left as an open question with several <i>possible </i>answers (e.g., natural laws, or godlike spiritual entities) but nothing conclusive.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is not just an m20 thing. Previous books literally spell it out that the consensus merely &quot;affects&quot; reality rather than defining it. It's not something that you can easily get from just the core rulebooks,but the books who are heavy on metaphysics do explain it.<br /> <br /> For instance, it is my personal belief that the technocracy did no create atoms and mitochondria. The Hermetics are not making up True names and Enochian, Reincarnations is objectively true etc.In fact, i think one book explicitly says that this is the case","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-29T14:58:03-07:00","id":1510126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509871-what-would-you-like-implemented-into-m5?p=1509904#post1509904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First and foremost: a major goal that I would set for M5 is a drastically reduced page count compared to M20. If you can get it down below 2e, even better.<br /> <br /> That means that you need to be extremely choosey about what goes into it. That <i>alone</i> is reason not to include anything about Foundations or Pillars in the core book. Ditto with things like the Technocratic Sphere variants and Minor Spheres: if anything like that gets included at all, it should come in supplements.</div> </div> </div> </div>What novel and additional Minor Spheres would you consider as nice and worthy to define / to include in books and supplements of World of Darkness M5 ? Including of course some specific and particular for Technocrats, Nephandi, Taftani, Ahi-i-Batini, or Solificati ; just to mention a few groups / factions. Any thoughts, drafts, or ideas ? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-01T05:02:31-07:00","id":1510345,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509871-what-would-you-like-implemented-into-m5?p=1510121#post1510121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is not just an m20 thing. Previous books literally spell it out that the consensus merely &quot;affects&quot; reality rather than defining it. It's not something that you can easily get from just the core rulebooks,but the books who are heavy on metaphysics do explain it.<br /> <br /> For instance, it is my personal belief that the technocracy did no create atoms and mitochondria. The Hermetics are not making up True names and Enochian, Reincarnations is objectively true etc.In fact, i think one book explicitly says that this is the case</div> </div> </div> </div>Previous books also literally spell out that the consensus does define reality. This is one of a few areas where the books contradict themselves because the writers are not on the same page. This has led to a number of different interpretations, all of which work at the gaming table even if they would be contradictory in universe.<br /> <br /> Instead of focusing on which one is objectively right, I would make it clear that Mages don't actually know but have very strong opinions on the matter. That is, I would voice several of these interpretations as in universe stances the factions in the Ascension War take. So the idea that physics as we understand it in the modern world is more or less the baseline of reality if the consensus is swept away would be a common view among the Technocracy. Meanwhile, a common opinion among the Traditions is that there are multiple realities which exist at once, with the Consensus determining which one is in ascendency and filling in the details.<br /> <br /> The idea that reality is completely determined by the consensus and there are few if any true Earthly Foundations would usually show up in Mages teetering on the edge of megalomania or really bad Quiets. It's my favorite interpretation of Mage, but I don't think its a healthy opinion in universe.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509871-what-would-you-like-implemented-into-m5?p=1510080#post1510080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've long been of the opinion that Mage only works if you allow for the possibility that the Consensus <i>isn't </i>the be-all and end-all of reality. M20 addresses this with its Earthly Foundations, where there are certain aspects of reality that will be true even if the locals believe otherwise; though those truths oughtn't be as specific as \u201cthe laws of physics as understood by modern scientists are true\u201d. They should be more broad-brush facts like \u201cthings fall down when you drop them\u201d and \u201cwater flows downhill\u201d. But even things like Newton's observation that the motions of the celestial bodies are described by the same mathematics as falling apples would be more of a Focus element rather than a fundamental truth: scientists see germs through their microscopes because that's what their paradigm says that they'll see, not because germs are actually real.</div> </div> </div> </div>This one, I think, would compete for the first or second most common viewpoint among the Traditions and probably second most common among the Technocracy as well. Though I think both would drop the part about evidence not being real. By its very nature that couldn't be proven in universe and Mages are more likely to assume they have more control rather than less.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-01T08:09:41-07:00","id":1510362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509871-what-would-you-like-implemented-into-m5?p=1510345#post1510345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Previous books also literally spell out that the consensus does define reality. This is one of a few areas where the books contradict themselves because the writers are not on the same page. This has led to a number of different interpretations, all of which work at the gaming table even if they would be contradictory in universe.<br /> <br /> Instead of focusing on which one is objectively right, I would make it clear that Mages don't actually know but have very strong opinions on the matter. That is, I would voice several of these interpretations as in universe stances the factions in the Ascension War take. So the idea that physics as we understand it in the modern world is more or less the baseline of reality if the consensus is swept away would be a common view among the Technocracy. Meanwhile, a common opinion among the Traditions is that there are multiple realities which exist at once, with the Consensus determining which one is in ascendency and filling in the details.<br /> <br /> The idea that reality is completely determined by the consensus and there are few if any true Earthly Foundations would usually show up in Mages teetering on the edge of megalomania or really bad Quiets. It's my favorite interpretation of Mage, but I don't think its a healthy opinion in universe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. And I'd go a step further and describe <i>both</i> of the absolutist positions from the earliest editions of the game as borderline Quiet positions: borderline Madness* in the case of the Traditions' stereotypical attitude that you outlined above, and borderline Denial in the case of the Technocracy's stereotypical \u201cMagick isn't real!\u201d attitude. <br /> <br /> That said, I'd also want M5 to emphasize that the Marauders and Nephandi aren't factions, per se: to the extent that factions still feature in M5, I'd want them to be the Traditions, the Technocracy, and the Disparates. Nephandi and Marauders would be better represented as \u201cinfections\u201d, or states of being: Nephandi are defined by the inverted Avatar rather than by an affiliation, and Marauders are defined by a weaponized permanent Quiet rather than by an affiliation. \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bFor instance, what <b>M20 Book of the Fallen</b> calls thr Mammonite faction would instead \u201cmerely\u201d be what happens when a Syndic inverts her Avatar; and the Dissidents in the Society of Ether should be as likely to be Marauders as not. <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:gray\">* \u2026or whatever M5 ends up calling it. I've noticed a push to avoid using the word \u201cMad\u201d in newer OPP products; and while Paradox isn't Onyx Path, I <i>do</i> see a case for renaming Madness in M5, as it really <i>isn't</i> about having a mental disorder; it's about connecting to reality in an unusual way. </span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509871-what-would-you-like-implemented-into-m5?p=1510345#post1510345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This one, I think, would compete for the first or second most common viewpoint among the Traditions and probably second most common among the Technocracy as well. Though I think both would drop the part about evidence not being real. By its very nature that couldn't be proven in universe and Mages are more likely to assume they have more control rather than less.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. I would like to see the \u201cevidence (obtained through Instruments) may in fact be a form of confirmation bias\u201d thing stated <i>somewhere</i>; but the tendency of mages to succumb to hubris would make it a tricky point to make. Perhaps a particularly self-aware Marauder could suggest it\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-01T08:40:04-07:00","id":1510365,"title":"","content":"Cleaned up spheres.<br /> polished combat mechanics <br /> better defined verbrenna <br /> Order of hermes revised","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-02T07:37:09-07:00","id":1510486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509871-what-would-you-like-implemented-into-m5?p=1510345#post1510345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Instead of focusing on which one is objectively right, I would make it clear that Mages don't actually know but have very strong opinions on the matter. That is, I would voice several of these interpretations as in universe stances the factions in the Ascension War take. \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah.<br /> <br /> A possible way to go about it, philosophically, would be to focus on the &quot;negativity&quot; elements in the mage experience from the Awakening onwards.<br /> <br /> *Instead of presenting Awakening as a moment of &quot;truth&quot; where one glimpses Reality(tm), one can focus on the &quot;Paradigm Shift&quot; element: the moment when the person's current understanding of the world, and/or their place in it, was shattered. That this is a moment of existential (if not ontological) aporia that either gets resolved trough Focus, or causes a fall into Denial/Madness (and not being a PC). So to speak: The days of Norman as &quot;the normal man&quot; have ended - what will the future depart?.<br /> <br /> *Then the book can explain how mages see the world using the 4 distinctions of the Tradition's Guide, where it explains how some mages are adamatly into their own set of beliefs, and think all of the rest are false, but most actually have a less constrained worldview where they can accept other forms of philosophy/magic as, at least, workable (maybe inferior, myabe dangerous, for some even equal). Focus not so much on how Paradigms could &quot;make sense&quot;, but rather on the gaps - you're a person that has an understanding of how reality works that's contested by other worldviews that also seem to function. A good place to start on how material proof in a wolrd with magic(k) can be far from infallible<br /> <br /> *A thing I wish, altrough it would be complicated to do (but one could argue it's now or never): Canonically sepparate the rules, the system, from the Lore.<br /> <br /> Mages knowing that Spheres exist was always a legacy from 1e. 1e Mage was a game that used to break the 4th wall, and it's characters were very saavy about the truth of the world - Awakening was understanding the actual Truth: that's why mages knew Focuses were a lie used to deceive reality, and a bit of a crutch for those with lower enlightenment. <br /> <br /> Mage has moverd from that, and them knowing their own system by name only generates nedless confusion. The system should be an abstract tool to represent and interact with the world, not the hidden truth of that world. Describe the system as a way to interact with the Focus, rather than the Focus as a way to interact with the system<br /> <br /> Now, I don't know <i>exactly how</i>. I know systems of &quot;dynamic magick&quot; that do what I want (Powered by Apocalipse has some very &quot;de-coupled&quot;, yet dynamic, systems), but aren't very portable to mage.<br /> <br /> Importing Awakening mechanics are a step in the right direction because they're more polished, but their Lore does declare the supernal truth of their system and I don't think M5 should copy <i>that</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I've noticed a push to avoid using the word \u201cMad\u201d in newer OPP products; and while Paradox isn't Onyx Path, I <i>do</i> see a case for renaming Madness in M5, as it really <i>isn't</i> about having a mental disorder; it's about connecting to reality in an unusual way.<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, IF the game moves away from the metaphisical trinity, we wouldn't need 3 types of Silence anymore. We could have a unified rule including all that was interesting about the types as posibilities of the same phenomena under an umbrella name.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 05-02-2023, 10:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-02T07:51:32-07:00","id":1510489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509871-what-would-you-like-implemented-into-m5?p=1510486#post1510486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, IF the game moves away from the metaphisical trinity, we wouldn't need 3 types of Silence anymore. We could have a unified rule including all that was interesting about the types as posibilities of the same phenomena under an umbrella name.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThat's actually how it worked before the Revised edition \u2014 except that they treated all Quiets the way MRev treated Madness.<br /> <br /> That, and my inclination would be to move away from the Metaphysical Trinity \u2014 but also to move <i>toward </i>the fourfold division of the Avatar Essences: Dynamic, Pattern, Primordial, and Questing. M20 already does this with its optional Resonance rules, with four broad types of Resonance that correspond to the four Essences: Temperamental goes with Dynamic; Stabilizing goes with Pattern; Elemental goes with Primordial; and Devotional goes with Questing.<br /> <br /> I could see reworking the different kinds of Quiet to conform to this arrangement as well: Madness and Denial work well as the Quiets aligned with Dynamic and Pattern Essences (though maybe Delusion might be a better term than Madness); you'd need only ditch Morbidity in favor of types of Quiet aligned with Primordial and Questing Essences. I could see the former being something like Obsession, where the mage fixates on some primordial element of reality (such as death) to an unhealthy degree (that is, Morbidity would merely be one possible kind of Obsession, just as Jhor is just one possible kind of Elemental Resonance); and the Quiet corresponding to a Questing Essence might be Hubris: the sense of one's own righteousness that invites a sense that you can do no wrong.<br /> <br /> So the four kinds of Quiet would be Delusion, Denial, Obsession, and Hubris.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509871-what-would-you-like-implemented-into-m5?p=1510486#post1510486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah.<br /> A possible way to go about it, philosophically, would be to focus on the &quot;negativity&quot; elements in the mage experience from the Awakening onwards.<br /> <br /> *Instead of presenting Awakening as a moment of &quot;truth&quot; where one glimpses Reality(tm), one can focus on the &quot;Paradigm Shift&quot; element: the moment when the person's current understanding of the world, and/or their place in it, was shattered. That this is a moment of existential (if not ontological) aporia that either gets resolved trough Focus, or causes a fall into Denial/Madness (and not being a PC). So to speak: The days of Norman as &quot;the normal man&quot; have ended - what will the future depart?.<br /> <br /> *Then the book can explain how mages see the world using the 4 distinctions of the Tradition's Guide, where it explains how some mages are adamatly into their own set of beliefs, and think all of the rest are false, but most actually have a less constrained worldview where they can accept other forms of philosophy/magic as, at least, workable (maybe inferior, myabe dangerous, for some even equal). Focus not so much on how Paradigms could &quot;make sense&quot;, but rather on the gaps - you're a person that has an understanding of how reality works that's contested by other worldviews that also seem to function. A good place to start on how material proof in a wolrd with magic(k) can be far from infallible</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed on all points \u2014 though I'd emphasize that many mages don't worry about such things, because they don't try to say that their Focus explains everything. Even the Technocracy (outside of a few 1e-style nuts that I'd classify as being firmly in Denial) takes the line of \u201cthere's Science, which we practice and which we think is superior; and there's Magick, which the Superstitionists practice and which is dangerous\u201d. And the Crafts generally go with \u201chere's how Magick works <i>for my Craft. </i>How it works for you, I neither know nor care.\u201d For the most part, only the Traditions pursue the notion that all Magicks are merely different flavors of the same thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509871-what-would-you-like-implemented-into-m5?p=1510486#post1510486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*A thing I wish, altrough it would be complicated to do (but one could argue it's now or never): Canonically sepparate the rules, the system, from the Lore.<br /> <br /> Mages knowing that Spheres exist was always a legacy from 1e. 1e Mage was a game that used to break the 4th wall, and it's characters were very saavy about the truth of the world - Awakening was understanding the actual Truth: that's why mages knew Focuses were a lie used to deceive reality, and a bit of a crutch for those with lower enlightenment.<br /> <br /> Mage has moved from that, and them knowing their own system by name only generates nedless confusion. The system should be an abstract tool to represent and interact with the world, not the hidden truth of that world. <b>Describe the system as a way to interact with the Focus, rather than the Focus as a way to interact with the system</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. In particular, it's what I was trying to say when I suggested that M5 ought to put Focus up front instead of relegating it to almost being an afterthought.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509871-what-would-you-like-implemented-into-m5?p=1510486#post1510486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, I don't know exactly how. I know systems of &quot;dynamic magick&quot; that do what I want (Powered by Apocalipse has some very &quot;de-coupled&quot;, yet dynamic, systems), but aren't very portable to mage.<br /> <br /> Importing Awakening mechanics are a step in the right direction because they're more polished, but their Lore does declare the supernal truth of their system and I don't think M5 should copy that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. I could see someone use the metaphysics of <b>Awakening</b> as a Focus in <b>Ascension</b>; but it would merely be one Focus among many; no more or less important than any other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 05-02-2023, 11:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-03T17:02:48-07:00","id":1510649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509871-what-would-you-like-implemented-into-m5?p=1510365#post1510365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cleaned up spheres.<br /> polished combat mechanics<br /> better defined verbrenna<br /> Order of hermes revised</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you define what you mean by cleaned up spheres, better defined verbena, and Order of Hermes revised ? Are you talking about the uhm Tradition book order of Hermes revised? It actually exists lol. (its horrible as far as i am concerned but it does exist)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-03T21:23:53-07:00","id":1510673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509871-what-would-you-like-implemented-into-m5?p=1510649#post1510649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Can you define what you mean by cleaned up spheres, better defined verbena, and Order of Hermes revised ? Are you talking about the uhm Tradition book order of Hermes revised? It actually exists lol. (its horrible as far as i am concerned but it does exist)</div> </div> </div> </div>The verbena have also been rather vaguely defined as the nature/pagany mages the trouble us they're genrally quite vaguely written in terms of what they believe and typically quire disconnected with pagan traditions and concepts<br /> <br /> Order of hermes revised has a more positive spin on.thr order. For some reason previous editions is obsessed with them being complete bastards. If your wizard classic order is all saruman the white then this is going to leave you frustrated if you're trying to play gandalf or Harry Potter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-04T01:07:09-07:00","id":1510689,"title":"","content":"What would I like from a fifth edition Mage: The Ascension? <br /> Don't use the 5th edition rules. Go back to something closer to V1,2,Rev or 20th. I like target difficulties. Just get rid of the superfluous combat rolls and it'll be rad. <br /> <br /> Mage specific? <br /> I want a well laid out and succinct explanation of how magic works in M5. <br /> <br /> I want the traditions to be discussed fairly. The OoH are the glue that holds the traditions together because they've got the magical philosophy that best works with other practices. They're more willing to compromise on an ideological level. Yes, that can make them arrogant but they literally have the most inclusive view of all the Traditions and that should count for something. <br /> <br /> Name changes for the Traditions should be more conservative. Some of the names are bad enough that a retcon is warranted, and some Traditions are progressive enough that they might actually change something, but Traditions by their very nature are conservative and will have the bulk of their members resist any name changes. <br /> <br /> The disparates are the disparates because they don't get along with others. any alliance of these fellows should at most extend to information sharing and the ability to move in another's territory unmolested. Perhaps they're more likely to sell one another services. It's going to be a convenience thing if it exists at all. <br /> <br /> <br /> Some minor things: <br /> I want HIT-Marks to have a reasonable naming scheme. I really like these guys, but given HIT1 is a clay golem, HIT2 is clockwork, HIT3 is steampunk, HIT4 is a robot, HIT5 a T800 like android, and HIT6 is a T1000 nanomachine cluster, I think M20 had a HIT9 or 10 that was more HIT5 refinement... Like, I know there are RL examples of companies being shit at keeping to a naming scheme, eg Microsoft Windows, but given iteration X is like 100% engineers and no marketing you'd think they'd be more anal with this kinda thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-04T06:29:52-07:00","id":1510699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509871-what-would-you-like-implemented-into-m5?p=1510673#post1510673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The verbena have also been rather vaguely defined as the nature/pagany mages the trouble us they're genrally quite vaguely written in terms of what they believe and typically quire disconnected with pagan traditions and concepts.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's because at the start the Verbena weren't pagan traditions, they were Ancient Alien followers dressed up as generic witches. I've gone into this in detail elsewhere, but many of the Traditions started as loose stereotypes artificially unified by backdating 19th and 20th century occult movements (or maybe as modern occult movements squeezed through a magical stereotype, who knows).<br /> <br /> I agree it would be good to remove that holdover, but it will require the thoughtful rework of each Tradition's history.<br /> <br /> <br /> In addition, I would like to see consistency with how the Sphere System is used. I agree with everyone who has said separate the system from in universe focuses. I'll expand that to cover a specific maddening issue: No more adding arbitrary Spheres by feel. I'm talking about how a standard spell like fireball suddenly needs Spirit if a Shaman is casting it or Mind if a psychic is. Or requiring Life to target something living when you don't need need Matter to cast the same spell on an object. The books are full of examples where a spell arbitrarily needs more Spheres than it would if you constructed the exact same effect using base rules and there's no reason why other than it sounds good. No adding a sphere unless the sphere is actually doing something.<br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-04T12:37:39-07:00","id":1510715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509871-what-would-you-like-implemented-into-m5?p=1510120#post1510120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thinking of how you could evolve / re-conceptualize lore for M5, and taking some notes from V5, I'd place both the Technocracy and the Traditions as an old crumbling order which is descending into Civil War as the Nephandi reveal the full extent of their infiltration into both Sleeper and Mage society.<br /> <br /> The Consensus start crumbling, and more and more Extraordinary Tech introduced into the Sleeper World backfires and creates potential Widderslainte. Traditions are having a very similar problem, as their efforts in rebuilding a post-Technocracy Consensus collide with millenarism, and more and more Marauders emerge.<br /> <br /> The two main factions are split into a tragic divide: many of their frontline troops are desperately holding out, , but many among the highest ranks are openly thinking Earth as lost. Archmages and Control are openly speaking of evacuating what of the Human Race might be salvaged into Horizon Realms.<br /> <br /> Will you fight to create pockets of &quot;safe and stable&quot; Reality, stopping the descent of your place into madness and corruption, or will you start exploring new realms in which start over?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> IMHO, any future installment of Mage should no longuer give that much importance to nephandi.<br /> <br /> Sure, the nephandi infiltrating is a thing since at least 2nd edition, but M20 turned that to 11.<br /> <br /> This factions does evil things? Nephandi. Your master is a dick? Nephandi. You burned your toast this morning? Nephandi.<br /> <br /> It frankly undermine the themes of the game, reducing what was a conflict of ideals that can go wrong to &quot;we've been corrupt by the stereotypical chaotic evil wizard&quot;.<br /> <br /> The technocracy doesn't need to have nephandi executives to polgrom the hell out of Crafts or to brainwash people. These are the logical consequences of it's values and policies since centuries.<br /> <br /> It's also pretty unbelievable, without puns, since M20 destroyed the cohesion of the nephandi. They were previously supernaturally inverted people who are deeply in adoration of various evil forces. Now M20 is specific that the Caul makes them sociopath.<br /> <br /> And sociopaths are not really capable of accuratly working together for anything, let alone infiltrating secret societies.<br /> <br /> It also demands a lot of unexplained ignorance for factions that are mages. No, Brucato, writing &quot;you'd like to know?&quot; For the aura of a nephandi act as if they're master infiltrators in fine doesn't hide the fact that any faction with members at least disciples in the mind sphere could pear into their members' minds to find who's a hidden sociopath with reality anihilating views.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-04T15:57:47-07:00","id":1510728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509871-what-would-you-like-implemented-into-m5?p=1510673#post1510673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The verbena have also been rather vaguely defined as the nature/pagany mages the trouble us they're genrally quite vaguely written in terms of what they believe and typically quire disconnected with pagan traditions and concepts<br /> <br /> Order of hermes revised has a more positive spin on.thr order. For some reason previous editions is obsessed with them being complete bastards. If your wizard classic order is all saruman the white then this is going to leave you frustrated if you're trying to play gandalf or Harry Potter.</div> </div> </div> </div>During an interview with the writers for <b>Lore of the Traditions</b>, it was mentioned that one of the instructions they were given was \u201cif there's anything about your Tradition that doesn't make sense, go ahead and blame the Order of Hermes for it.\u201d Tellingly, I think this was mentioned in conjunction with the writer of the Verbena chapter; so I get to address two of your points at once.<br /> <br /> My own preference is to just downplay the Traditions so that it doesn't matter as much if their portrayals are good or bad; because the main focus would be on the personal struggles of individual mages instead. And frankly, that's how I've tended to play the game from the get-go, even back in the days when the assumption was that the protagonists are all part of the Traditions: I took the decentralized nature of the Traditions as a basis for saying that the protagonists are, in practice, on their own even if they were nominally members of an organization.<br /> <br /> Rather than getting a 5e revision to the Verbena to make them more defined and to connect them more with pagan traditions and concepts, I'd much rather get something like the <b>Paradigm Explored</b> series of Storyteller's Vault products (currently at three books: <b>Wyrd and Weft</b>, <b>Number and Shape</b>, and <b>Fairy-Faith</b>) that focuses on giving some insight on just what those pagan traditions and concepts <i>are</i>, in a way that will enable me to make a believable witch. Similarly with the Order of Hermes: if you downplay the importance of the Traditions in general, and of Traditions politics in particular, them all you really need is a <b>Paradigm Explored</b> for Hermetic views on magick. You want to play Gandalf or Harry Potter? Go for it! All you have to do is not insist that they belong to the Order of Hermes or partake in whatever shenanigans it may or may not be involved in.<br /> <hr /><br /> That is, stop treating \u201cWizard\u201d as a synonym for \u201cOrder of Hermes\u201d, and \u201cWitch\u201d as a synonym for \u201cVerbena\u201d. Keep a few references in there for those who want to use the Traditions; but make it something optional. For instance, <b>Paradigm Explored: Number and Shape</b> has a section in it about what Tradition or Convention the sample character might belong to; and VA is near the top of the list. But so are NWO and ItX, as well as Order of Hermes and a few others (Celestial Chorus, Syndicate, and Hollow Ones). And there's nothing saying that the character has to belong to <i>any</i> of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 05-04-2023, 07:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-04T16:09:35-07:00","id":1510729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509871-what-would-you-like-implemented-into-m5?p=1510699#post1510699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">n addition, I would like to see consistency with how the Sphere System is used. I agree with everyone who has said separate the system from in universe focuses. I'll expand that to cover a specific maddening issue: No more adding arbitrary Spheres by feel. I'm talking about how a standard spell like fireball suddenly needs Spirit if a Shaman is casting it or Mind if a psychic is. Or requiring Life to target something living when you don't need need Matter to cast the same spell on an object. The books are full of examples where a spell arbitrarily needs more Spheres than it would if you constructed the exact same effect using base rules and there's no reason why other than it sounds good. No adding a sphere unless the sphere is actually doing something.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. This is one of the things I'd be borrowing from <b>Awakened</b>: the design philosophy that conjunctional effects should be <i>rare</i>, and the sort of thing that requires special justification (like \u201cyou need both Life and Matter if you want to transform something that's living into something that isn't, or vice versa\u201d, or \u201cyou need to add a couple of dots of Correspondence to an Effect if you want to use Sympathetic Links\u201d). <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-04T17:12:41-07:00","id":1510736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509871-what-would-you-like-implemented-into-m5?p=1510673#post1510673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The verbena have also been rather vaguely defined as the nature/pagany mages the trouble us they're genrally quite vaguely written in terms of what they believe and typically quire disconnected with pagan traditions and concepts<br /> <br /> Order of hermes revised has a more positive spin on.thr order. For some reason previous editions is obsessed with them being complete bastards. If your wizard classic order is all saruman the white then this is going to leave you frustrated if you're trying to play gandalf or Harry Potter.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the Verbena books explicitly says that they are NOT as a matter of fact, meant to be a representation of real cultures. That is, it's a feature, not a bug&quot;<br /> <br /> I know how Order of Hermes revised is written, but i am confused as to what you want. If i am not mistaken m20 does keep the fall of doissetep, and the other events that IC created OH revised.<br /> You want another book like that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-04T21:27:58-07:00","id":1510755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509871-what-would-you-like-implemented-into-m5?p=1510736#post1510736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the Verbena books explicitly says that they are NOT as a matter of fact, meant to be a representation of real cultures. That is, it's a feature, not a bug&quot;<br /> <br /> I know how Order of Hermes revised is written, but i am confused as to what you want. If i am not mistaken m20 does keep the fall of doissetep, and the other events that IC created OH revised.<br /> You want another book like that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes but that's a bad thing. They're vague and suffer for it.<br /> <br /> I just explained what I want, i want a characterization from the revised edition as a more opermistic approach the order. M20 is meta neutral. I'd like it to continue on with that characterisation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-05T06:56:24-07:00","id":1510781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509871-what-would-you-like-implemented-into-m5?p=1510729#post1510729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Agreed. This is one of the things I'd be borrowing from <b>Awakened</b>: the design philosophy that conjunctional effects should be <i>rare</i>, and the sort of thing that requires special justification (like \u201cyou need both Life and Matter if you want to transform something that's living into something that isn't, or vice versa\u201d, or \u201cyou need to add a couple of dots of Correspondence to an Effect if you want to use Sympathetic Links\u201d).</div> </div> </div> </div>I was struck by that myself when I was writing the last post. When you strip out all the arbitrary extra spheres many spells drop down to only one or two spheres, and most of the two sphere cases come from very specific things: transmutation, something from nothing, locking, range, etc. It made it clear why Awakening is so frugal with the Spheres.<br /> <br /> Awakening stripped a few more things out (you don't need Prime for manifesting something from nothing, for instance) so a frugal Ascension would have conjunctional effects pop up slightly more often, but still much more rarely than they seem to do now.<br /> <br /> Edit: Removed the chart. It needs a step or two added.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":". 05-05-2023, 11:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-05T12:07:45-07:00","id":1510809,"title":"","content":"I took a quick skim through the main nine Spheres writeups in M20 and noted every place that a Sphere suggests the need for a pattern Sphere. These seem to come in five flavors:<br /> <br /> 1) The spell is a transmutation or grafting so both spheres are primary<br /> <br /> 2) The pattern sphere is a locking sphere<br /> <br /> 3) The pattern sphere is a technically optional but functionally necessary modifier to the main spell.<br /> <br /> 4) The pattern sphere is actually the main effect which is being modified<br /> <br /> 5) The pattern sphere is being used to target<br /> \u200b<br /> 1 and 2 are clearly part of the rules. 4 is as well, just from a different direction. 3 is not specifically covered, but is a logical extension.<br /> <br /> The largest chunk of sphere addons, though, comes from arbitrary targeting requirements that aren't in the rules. Instead they seem to be based on the assumption of a rule that sounds like it would exist but doesn't and doesn't have any reason to. Targeting is an extremely iffy reason to add a sphere and I would drop virtually all examples of it.<br /> <br /> I'd also take a careful look at all examples of 4. Two of the four of them are nonsense. If Telekinesis were listed in Forces it would be easier to see that Mind isn't doing anything in the spell. Because it is listed in Mind we can easily miss that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-05T17:27:50-07:00","id":1510841,"title":"","content":"I would like to see mage Factions presented less childish and more serious. As a random example, i was reading about the solificati ,in book of crafts and eventually came across something along the lines of &quot;modern children of knowledge are more likely to be inspired by Timothy Leary, than the traditional alchemist stereotypes&quot; Ok this is not an exact quote but its a good summarization i think.<br /> I am not saying that these people should disappear completely, but i really wish they were not presented as the norm of their factions. The solificati are just one example, this thing is everywhere.<br /> <br /> Also, i wish that m5 does not fawn over certain traditions. For instance, almost every single thing written about the Cult of ecstacy is about how any and all stereotypes you have about them is wrong, excluding a few rotten apples( who barely get any mention at all). Forget about their tradition book, this is everywhere.<br /> But speaking of the Tradition book, well, normally splatbooks are in-universe propaganda...but reading theirs, especially second edition, i get the impression that it was written OOC by the IC narrator lol.<br /> <br /> In general, i would also present the Traditions as less good than what they are currently portrayed,say, -1 point of humanity on average (though of course, good people will still exist)<br /> <br /> In fact, i wish Ascension itself was more in the background. I find it weird that almost every single mage believes in it, especially in regards to mass ascension. I sometimes think that IC this whole thing was made viral by some cynical masters who noted that &quot;fight so i can be a wizard king once more&quot; made people less likely to throw their lives than &quot;fight for Ascension&quot;, but even taking that into account, its just strange. In general most people in this world with great power seek to either a) gain even more or b)provide services and protection to their community/humanity or some variation there of.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, while its not going to happen i would actually make the Nephandi a playable faction, albeit with the understanding that they, or at least some factions of them, would be changed to resemble more the Baali or the circle of Red.<br /> <br /> Mind you, i will eat my own hand if even the least controversial of these changes was included. but hey, maybe Santa will read it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-05T17:36:47-07:00","id":1510842,"title":"","content":"The quest for Ascension is another one of those things that I like to relegate mostly to the Traditions, along with the whole \u201cit's all just different flavors of the same thing, man\u2026\u201d attitude that the earliest editions featured. Maybe not as heavily as the latter; but its near-ubiquity in earlier editions of the game can be chalked up in retrospect to the Traditions being the default protagonists in the first three editions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-05T17:54:11-07:00","id":1510843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509871-what-would-you-like-implemented-into-m5?p=1510842#post1510842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The quest for Ascension is another one of those things that I like to relegate mostly to the Traditions, along with the whole \u201cit's all just different flavors of the same thing, man\u2026\u201d attitude that the earliest editions featured. Maybe not as heavily as the latter; but its near-ubiquity in earlier editions of the game can be chalked up in retrospect to the Traditions being the default protagonists in the first three editions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even in the context of the traditions I wish It was a bit more in the background sort of how it was (I think, though I might be wrong), in the Sorcerer's Crusade. <br /> It should be a thing mind you, but not The thing. Especially the concept of mass ascension. <br /> <br /> Also I want to see an end to the idea that there can only be one tradition per sphere. From a Realpolitik perspective it is stupid. Granted I don't think the books say &quot;the dreamspeakers would stop the Wu lung from entering&quot; but I wish it were more explicit","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-05T18:22:45-07:00","id":1510844,"title":"","content":"That was ended in M20, by downplaying to irrelevance the idea that there's <i>any</i> connection between Traditions and Spheres. They don't flat-out say that the are no Seats of Matter, Entropy, Forces, etc.; but they don't mention such things, either.<br /> <br /> As for the first part: as I said before, I don't have strong opinions about reworking the Traditions, because I'd prefer that M5 take what M20 started in removing the Traditions as the focus of the game and run with it. In M5 as I imagine it, you don't play a member of the Traditions by default; you do so because you have decided that you want your mage to partake of the culture that defines the Traditions. And that culture is one part \u201ccan't we all just get along?\u201d and one part \u201cthe purpose of a mage is to grow beyond her limits and Ascend\u201d.<br /> <br /> That is, rather than existing to provide a set of archetypal approaches to Magick, the M5 Traditions would exist solely to facilitate people who want to play Mage the way it was played in the first three editions; if you want to get away from that sort of thing, just don't have your mage align herself with the Traditions. More generally, make membership in an arcane Society an opt-in thing rather than an opt-out thing. You don't play a Hermetic; you play a wizard. And if you choose to have your wizard join the Order of Hermes, that's an option you can take. But you don't have to; and it's not assumed that you will.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 05-05-2023, 09:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-05T19:30:35-07:00","id":1510850,"title":"","content":"Please finally give us rules for creating and transforming individual spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-06T03:23:56-07:00","id":1510872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509871-what-would-you-like-implemented-into-m5?p=1510841#post1510841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would like to see mage Factions presented less childish and more serious. As a random example, i was reading about the solificati ,in book of crafts and eventually came across something along the lines of &quot;modern children of knowledge are more likely to be inspired by Timothy Leary, than the traditional alchemist stereotypes&quot; Ok this is not an exact quote but its a good summarization i think.</div> </div> </div> </div>What exactly is childish about that? I mean, I'm not saying you have to like it, but it seems a fairly reasonable direction to take an alchemical faction. It's taking a traditional idea and connecting it up to a modern strand of esotericism.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For instance, almost every single thing written about the Cult of ecstacy is about how any and all stereotypes you have about them is wrong, excluding a few rotten apples( who barely get any mention at all). Forget about their tradition book, this is everywhere.<br /> But speaking of the Tradition book, well, normally splatbooks are in-universe propaganda...but reading theirs, especially second edition, i get the impression that it was written OOC by the IC narrator lol. </div> </div> </div>I came away with the complete opposite view. Revised especially seemed entirely about the conflict between those who follow the Code of Ananda and those who don't. There's an entire faction of them. Seemed very clear that plenty of Cultists do in fact cross the line; that the Code is somewhat artificial whilst also being necessary to stop the Tradition becoming totally monstrous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-07T02:14:03-07:00","id":1510967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509871-what-would-you-like-implemented-into-m5?p=1510872#post1510872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What exactly is childish about that? I mean, I'm not saying you have to like it, but it seems a fairly reasonable direction to take an alchemical faction. It's taking a traditional idea and connecting it up to a modern strand of esotericism.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I came away with the complete opposite view. Revised especially seemed entirely about the conflict between those who follow the Code of Ananda and those who don't. There's an entire faction of them. Seemed very clear that plenty of Cultists do in fact cross the line; that the Code is somewhat artificial whilst also being necessary to stop the Tradition becoming totally monstrous.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its not really something that is easy to articulate by pointing to a specific page. I basically feel more like a mage sometimes when playing a blood mage or a mortal sorcerer lol. There is a certain seriousness missing in some writeups of certain factions. As in, someone had a very weird view of what it means to be young lol.<br /> <br /> Then again, i have been recently reading a lot of 2ebooks (m20 is written to a huge extend from a 2nd ed perspective), so i may be biased.<br /> <br /> If you own it, read 2nd edition cult of ecstacy.<br /> <br /> Even if revised is better( and it may be), i am not sure i follow your logic. I know about the &quot;dissidents&quot; to ananda, but do they actually appear outside the &quot;here are the baddies&quot; section of the Trad book?<br /> In essence, think of every time that a book talks about an ecstatic. Then, presume that i have a gun pointed towards you and i ask you &quot;from which faction is he?&quot; Assuming you pass your darwin test you will say &quot;Uhm, a joybringer or discordian or..&quot; and so on.<br /> One almost gets the idea that the actual ancient philosophies behind ecstacy are an afterthought (unless, again, i have been spending too much time readding 2e books)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-07T02:19:30-07:00","id":1510968,"title":"","content":"Both 2e and M20 were written by Phil \u201cSatyros\u201d Brucato, who has said on record that when he was writing the original Cult of Ecstasy Tradition Book, he found himself identifying with them \u2014 thus, \u201cSatyros\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-07T03:24:54-07:00","id":1510969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509871-what-would-you-like-implemented-into-m5?p=1510968#post1510968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Both 2e and M20 were written by Phil \u201cSatyros\u201d Brucato, who has said on record that when he was writing the original Cult of Ecstasy Tradition Book, he found himself identifying with them \u2014 thus, \u201cSatyros\u201d.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well,yeah, i know. If there were an m5 i wish a bit more, uhm subtlety on likes/dislikes.<br /> I only mentioned the cult as an example by the way. I wish the same for all other traditions/factions","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-13T11:17:54-07:00","id":1511553,"title":"","content":"The Universal Practices of Awakening are one of the best additions to the great Mage Saga (coming all the way back from Ars Magica). So something of the sort would be top notch.<br /> I prefer the Arcanes of Awakening too; exemplified by how making a necromancer in Ascension is really contrived, and a game of mages should have all the well-know magic archetypes easy to access. But since the 9 Spheres are so entrenched in the setting, I don't see them getting changed.<br /> <br /> I've always had the impression too, as has been said in the thread, that playing a sorcerer in Vampire is generally more magical than in Mage, and that is messed up. Mage can sometime be way too superhero magic and powers, instead of the crafting of spells, the incantation of reality and the changing of the world by will. <br /> There is also the matter that the setting, for me, doesn't have a solid ground for a diverse set of chronicles. The War of Ascension is way too front and center, and is way too heated for any character-focus, politics and investigation. A problem similar to Werewolf and Vampire's 3rd edition imo. Either a setting where there is no ticking clock or one with less openly belligerent factions would work best. Mage is a game chockfull of promises of exploration, of deeper meaning and understanding, but you can't really do that if you got a hundred Nephandi, Technocrats and Marauders breathing down your neck.<br /> <br /> So a return, or even creation, of a more provincial game of Mage would enrich the setting in my opinion. Fifth Edition of WoD seems to be going this route anyway, and it is really helping. The World of Darkness is very dark if everything you do and take part-in is a world-wide open-war conflict for good and evil. Lots of my players actually miss the small and human factor, in high and long Chronicles, when you end up dealing more and more with the supernatural, to the point of exclusivity.<br /> <br /> And yeah, Paradigm or Mage Archetype being the &quot;Predator Type&quot; of Mage could be fun. It would have to be a general practice and customs of your magic, though. Like a mage that deals in souls, one that heals, one for blood rituals, one that is merely lucky, hacktivist, shaman, etc... Simply because, when playing Mage, me and my friends always find it difficult to really feel like you are playing &quot;that type of mage&quot; you were wanting to play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-14T15:42:01-07:00","id":1511663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509871-what-would-you-like-implemented-into-m5?p=1510728#post1510728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is, stop treating \u201cWizard\u201d as a synonym for \u201cOrder of Hermes\u201d, and \u201cWitch\u201d as a synonym for \u201cVerbena\u201d. Keep a few references in there for those who want to use the Traditions; but make it something optional. For instance, <b>Paradigm Explored: Number and Shape</b> has a section in it about what Tradition or Convention the sample character might belong to; and VA is near the top of the list. But so are NWO and ItX, as well as Order of Hermes and a few others (Celestial Chorus, Syndicate, and Hollow Ones). And there's nothing saying that the character has to belong to <i>any</i> of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are Mages from the Cult of Ecstasy mentioned in this section as a good enough choice for a player's character ? Certainly since the start Ecstatics have been a distinct, complex, and characterful option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-14T17:29:02-07:00","id":1511678,"title":"","content":"They're not. But you can take that as a challenge: how would you adapt the Focus presented in <b>Number and Shape</b> to fit a Cultist of Ecstasy? My starting point would be the link between music and math: for example, chords are pleasing because of an inherent mathematical connection between the notes they're composed of. A Cultist would likely take the normal stereotype about math being boring and turn it on its head, seeking to find the beauty in math and the math in beauty, possibly starting with the art of music and then expanding to other fields of aesthetics. The Hollow Ones entry touches on this sort of thing (pointing to Lewis Carroll and Ada Lovelace as models for Hollow Ones with a deep interest in math, and suggesting the use of such things as haiku and sonnets in his magick).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 05-14-2023, 11:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-16T07:12:48-07:00","id":1511798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509871-what-would-you-like-implemented-into-m5?p=1511678#post1511678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're not. But you can take that as a challenge: how would you adapt the Focus presented in <b>Number and Shape</b> to fit a Cultist of Ecstasy? My starting point would be the link between music and math: for example, chords are pleasing because of an inherent mathematical connection between the notes they're composed of. A Cultist would likely take the normal stereotype about math being boring and turn it on its head, seeking to find the beauty in math and the math in beauty, possibly starting with the art of music and then expanding to other fields of aesthetics. The Hollow Ones entry touches on this sort of thing (pointing to Lewis Carroll and Ada Lovelace as models for Hollow Ones with a deep interest in math, and suggesting the use of such things as haiku and sonnets in his magick).</div> </div> </div> </div>Comes to mind :P:<br /> <img title=\"image.png\" data-tempid=\"temp_1241_1684245481960_757\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1241\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1241\" data-thumb-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1241&amp;type=thumb\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"image.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-need-data-att-update js-lightbox-participant\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> <br /> A CE could be a game developer and/or gamer, making/playing games that use geometry and require high concentration. Entering into rapport with the numbers and shapes involved through a medium more ludic than academic, but still playing to that idea of beauty in maths","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}